  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Islamic State Khorasan Province (ISKP, ISIS-K) was announced in January 2015 by former Pakistani Taliban and Afghan militants in Nangarhar. After losing most of its rural strongholds in Nangarhar and Kunar to US, Afghan government and Taliban pressure (2019-2020), it shifted to urban cells and mass-casualty attacks: the August 2021 Kabul airport bombing, attacks on Shia, Hazara and Sufi communities, the January 2024 Kerman bombing in Iran and the March 2024 Crocus City Hall attack near Moscow. It fights the Taliban, which has degraded its networks inside Afghanistan; UN monitors say it keeps a presence and recruits widely in Central Asia. In June 2026 the Taliban claimed airstrikes on ISKP sites inside Pakistan, which Pakistan denied. In the game ISIS-K appears as small mountain and urban cells in afghan_highlands, fighting both the player and the Taliban. Mass-casualty attacks exist only in briefing text, never as playable content.",
    "squad_size": 5,
    "fireteam": "Cells of 3-6 in towns, small mountain groups of 6-12 in the eastern provinces. In game: 2-3 battle-buddy pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Urban cells hiding in residential compounds, fighting room to room when raided",
      "Mountain ambushes on tracks in steep valleys (Kunar and Nangarhar-type terrain)",
      "IED hazards on roads and compound entrances, telegraphed for the player",
      "Targeted attacks on Taliban checkpoints, which the player can encounter as a three-way fight",
      "Motorbike scouts and couriers",
      "Fall back into crowded markets and villages, keeping the casualty rule active"
    ],
